[{:seon.task/name "one-monotonic-clock"
  :seon.task/plan "Done; what exists. Seon has one monotonic clock: `seon.profile/now-ns`, uncontracted (seon.profile is not metered), a Chez foreign read of clock_gettime_nsec_np(CLOCK_UPTIME_RAW), the clock every process shares (a forked child reads the same timeline): 9.5 ns a read, no allocation, 41 ns resolution on the M1, against Jolt's System/nanoTime at 102 ns and 225 bytes through its contract. `seon.profile/ms-since` is the one 'ms since t0' (it lives in seon.profile because seon.contract and seon.db cannot require seon.lib). `seon.lib/now-ns`, `seon.sock/now-ns` and every System/nanoTime in src and test are gone; the profiler's samples are no longer quantized to 1 us. v1: System/nanoTime on the JVM, one clock within one process. Wiki: docs/machine.md#the-clock."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.profile-test/the-clock-is-the-one-every-process-reads seon.profile-test/reading-the-clock-allocates-nothing seon.profile-test/every-touched-function-has-an-estimated-time}}
 {:seon.task/name "a-call-is-measured-one-way"
  :seon.task/plan "Owner, 2026-10-23: src resists growth so agents reuse and improve the core parts rather than making one-offs (DECISIONS). What exists: two measurements of one call. seon.repl/wrap-cost measures each evaluated form (wall ns by seon.profile/now-ns, allocated bytes, engine ticks counted in a finally inside jolt.host/ticks-of so a form that throws is counted, the costliest functions); seon.cost/once measures a cost proof's call (CPU ns, allocated bytes, ticks as ticks-of answers them, contracted calls). Correct: one seon.profile/measure! runs a function and answers its value, and hands what it measured ({:ticks :bytes :wall-ns :cpu-ns :calls}) to a callback from a finally, so a call that throws is measured and its exception goes on; the REPL and the cost proof each read what they show from it. A law keeps it one: no src form but measure! reads the tick counter (jolt.host/ticks-of or ticks). Deletes both inline measurements."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.profile-test/a-call-is-measured-one-way seon.main-test/only-measure-reads-the-tick-counter}}]
